# Cached line coverage, written by hk's `coverage` step in fix mode.
#
# WHY A CACHE: measuring costs a full instrumented test run, which is why
# coverage lives in the pre-push set and not in pre-commit. The README badge
# has to be regenerated on every commit, though, so `readme-badges` reads
# this instead of measuring. That is what makes it cheap enough for `fast`.
#
# key is a git SHA over the files that can MOVE coverage -- every tracked
# `*.rs`, plus SPEC.md and the fixtures, which the suite reads:
#
#   git ls-files -s -- '*.rs' SPEC.md tests/fixtures | git hash-object --stdin
#
# README.md is deliberately NOT in the key. It is REGENERATED from this
# file, so including it would make every badge update invalidate the cache
# that produced the badge -- a loop with no fixed point.
#
# If the key still matches, the number below is current by construction and
# no measurement is needed. If it does not, pre-push says so rather than
# trusting it.
key fd07e187ad1b0f2b91662cb23cc0fb70c2c77fdf
lines 98.05
